-  // ── THE SECOND SHEET (12 Aug) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
-  // Fifty-eight products, APPENDED rather than merged, and the distinction is
-  // deliberate. The header above says a new sheet should be re-run through the
-  // generator that produced the first seventy — but that script is not in this
-  // repository, and a reimplementation of its four derivations would silently
-  // alter rows that are already correct and already verified. The seventy above
-  // are untouched; only these are derived, and the shelf spec checks them in
-  // full, which is what the spec is for.
-  //
-  // WHAT THEY CLOSE. The shelf had no pharmacy-derm brands at all — the only
-  // group whose formulations carry published clinical evidence, and the group
-  // Indian dermatologists actually name. It also had no premium hair oil, the
-  // one empty cell in the tier grid. And, in monthly terms, nothing a face
-  // budget under ~₹650 could complete: the cheapest three-step routine was
-  // ₹642/month with sunscreen alone at ₹321. Large-pack mass SPF takes that
-  // floor to ₹318, which is the difference between a low budget being served
-  // and being apologised to.
-  //
-  // BOTH PHOTOGRAPHS ARE VERIFIED AND FROM DIFFERENT RETAILERS, resolved by
-  // script against live pages and checked for content-type — never guessed. A
-  // second picture from the same CDN as the first would die on the same day,
-  // which is the one thing the second picture exists to prevent.
