From 36f80b765d4e2ce20574c45551eff19655d9a0b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 18:44:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Every category is a step the routine can place
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The shelf went from 16 display categories to 55 and `classify()` ends in a
silent fallback — `{ step: 'Treat', rank: 45, 'Apply a thin, even layer.' }`.
Thirteen routine categories landed in it at once, 560 products: 166 facial
kits, 107 hair kits, 77 hair styling, 37 foot creams, 36 body oils, eye
creams, night creams, face scrubs, face oils, lip care, body masks, soap,
hair colour and hair removal, every one printed into a face routine as
"Treat · apply a thin, even layer".

Two did something worse than fall through. `/treatment/` was unanchored, so
"Hair treatment" and "Scalp treatment" matched the FACE rule thirty lines
above their own and were handed "a pea-sized amount over the whole face,
avoiding the eye area" — under a keratin smoothening treatment. That rule
also never matched anything it was written for: no sheet this shelf has
loaded produces a display category of exactly "Treatment", so it was dormant
its whole life and then woke up on the wrong products.

And `/shampoo/` matched "Dry shampoo", which reached the wash step and was
told to "rinse thoroughly" — the one instruction a dry shampoo must never be
given.

This is the SECOND time this exact failure has happened in this file. The
comment above the moisturiser rule records the first, when `/cream/` caught
"Hand cream" and put it above the body wash. Both times it was found by
looking. `every-category-is-a-step.spec.ts` is the test: every routine
category has a rule of its own, no group's rule reaches another group's
product, no rule repeats the fallback's text, and a built routine prints no
step on the fallback.

Hair kit and Hair extensions are declared SHOP_ONLY rather than given a step.
A kit is a bundle of steps and clip-ins are worn, not applied — there is no
honest instruction or frequency for either. They stay buyable in the Market.

Verified: 17 suites / 183 tests green. A planned routine for a combination
profile now returns Morning 5, Evening 3, Weekly 3, Body 4 — every band
filled, every step correctly ordered and instructed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TyRR86EpAZxHuzmiaaCyxP
